From d6f6fad0026644e3005dc59221ab2eab63028edd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:09:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] LOCAL: pvr: 16 MiB initial global free list on parameter
 format v1

Local patch for the GE8300 on amazon-sheldonp; not to be sent. The
firmware can't pause the PM to grow a free list on this core (the
PM_PAGE_MANAGEOP pause is never acknowledged), so an out-of-memory TA
ends in a GPU reset and page fault. Start large instead;
PVR_FREE_LIST_MB still overrides.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_device.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_device.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_device.c
index e60aae4fe97..5a646b0cca3 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_device.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_device.c
@@ -870,7 +870,14 @@ VkResult PVR_PER_ARCH(create_device)(struct pvr_physical_device *pdevice,
     * list, so an out-of-memory TA locks up; start big instead.
     */
    {
-      const int64_t mb = debug_get_num_option("PVR_FREE_LIST_MB", 0);
+      /* GE8300 (format v1): start with 16 MiB, since growing doesn't work. */
+      const int64_t mb = debug_get_num_option(
+         "PVR_FREE_LIST_MB",
+         PVR_GET_FEATURE_VALUE(&pdevice->dev_info,
+                               simple_parameter_format_version,
+                               0) == 1
+            ? 16
+            : 0);
 
       if (mb > 0)
          initial_free_list_size =
-- 
